<title>FINLAND: FINNISH ARAVA INTEREST RATES TO BE CUT IN APRIL.</title>
<headline>FINNISH ARAVA INTEREST RATES TO BE CUT IN APRIL.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interest rates on Finnish publicly subsidised Arava loans will be lowered from April 1, the Ministry of the Environment said in a statement on Thursday.</p>
<p>The maximum interest rate on loans for building apartments or houses and for renovation purposes will be lowered to 7.5 percent from 8.5 percent, the ministry said.</p>
<p>The top interest rate on loans for the construction of cooperatively-held apartment buildings and renovation of those will be lowered to 7.0 percent from 8.5 percent, it added.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 240, news@Reuters.fi</p>
